{
  "title": "How to Pass Creación Digital I — UEM 2026-27",
  "slides": [
    {"content":"<h1>How to Pass Creación Digital I</h1><h2>Universidad Europea de Madrid · UEM 2026-27</h2><p><strong>Rubén Vega Balbás, PhD</strong></p><p><em>6 ECTS · 150 h total · 80 h presencial contact · 70 h autonomous/tutoring/evaluation</em></p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Official course contract</h2><table><tr><th>Subject</th><td>Creación Digital I</td></tr><tr><th>Contact structure</th><td>10 h magistral · 20 h seminars · 8 h problem solving · 20 h projects · 14 h labs · 8 h debates</td></tr><tr><th>Contents</th><td>I.1–I.9: digital images, 2D tools, colour/bitmaps, effects, 3D form, volume, composition, animation, still life</td></tr></table>"},
    {"content":"<h2>How you pass</h2><p>You pass by making, explaining, and revising a portfolio of bounded digital artefacts. A polished image without source/process evidence is incomplete.</p><ul><li>Magistral and seminar preparation</li><li>Lab notebook with files, versions, accessibility and attribution checks</li><li>Individual problem-solving evidence</li><li>Project critique and final synthesis</li></ul>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Studio evidence</h2><p>Every project submission includes the artefact, editable/source files, process notes, tool/version notes, attribution, and a short human-authorship statement. AI assistance is declared by tool, contribution, and human verification.</p><p><strong>Research boundary:</strong> this is teaching evidence, not research data. No collection or exhibition without consent, DPO/institutional approval, and administration.</p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Evidence status</h2><p>Some I.2–I.9 pedagogy rows remain NONE or [BIBLIO-GAP]. Those units are taught as declared pilots: technical documentation may ground HOW, but it does not prove that a sequence produces learning outcomes.</p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Ordinary and extraordinary evaluation</h2><p>Use the official UEM guide and current subject documentation for the binding evaluation weights and dates. Indicative checkpoints may move. Failed evidence is repaired through a defined resubmission, not silently replaced by attendance.</p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Questions and next step</h2><p>Start with the unit forge, read the evidence row, complete the lab contract, and bring the process trail to critique. Ask before publishing a student artefact publicly.</p>"}
  ]
}
